## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the candidate's ability to design scalable, isolation-preserving authorization systems in streaming architectures. It covers critical cloud-native concepts including per-tenant policy governance, ABAC vs RBAC trade-offs, lightweight in-memory caches, policy versioning, and safe propagation of live policy updates without cross-tenant leakage.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy governance and attribute-based access control (ABAC)
- In-memory caching strategies with topic-scoped isolation
- Policy versioning and cryptographic signing for auditability
- Secure propagation mechanisms that prevent information leakage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo evaluator sketch
function evalPolicy(tenantId, resource, action, attrs) {
  const policy = cache.get(tenantId);
  if (!policy) return false;
  if (!policy.isCurrent()) {
    cache.refresh(tenantId); // async background refresh
    return false; // fail closed during refresh
  }
  return policy.evaluate({ resource, action, attrs });
}
```

